# EVERY SUPPLY THAT SAYS WHAT IT ACTUALLY SERVED, BESIDE WHAT IT COMMITTED AND HOW FAR IT CAN
# STRETCH. One row per layer filing a `pm:Jagged/draw` against a stated rating.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE THIRD OF THE LAYER'S THREE QUANTITIES, AND THE FIRST RELATION TO READ ONE.
#    `EliminationAgainst` names all three -- demand, nameplate, draw -- and says why the third
#    is there: "an implementation that eliminates demand and forgets the draw has silently
#    claimed a utilisation it did not observe". Seventeen draws are filed. Before this file the
#    only question anything asked of one was whether it was ABSENT -- epistemics/absences.sqlc
#    reads `draw_absent` -- and no relation anywhere read the value. The warning was executed.
#
# ⛔ THE DRAW IS NOT THE DEMAND, AND THE CORPUS SETTLES THAT RATHER THAN ASSUMING IT. They
#   agree at the mode in eight layers of seventeen and differ in nine, so a reader taking one
#   for the other is wrong more often than right. `capability` was asked for 6 and served 3.
#
# ⛔⛔ A DRAW ABOVE THE DEMAND IS NOT A DEFECT, WHICH IS WHY THIS FILE REPORTS AND DOES NOT
#    JUDGE. `merge-pt-member/linha-partilhada` draws 10 where its demand reaches 8.0 at most,
#    and the filing says why: "A PRODUÇÃO INTEIRA DA LINHA... a fatia do irmão está aqui
#    dentro, e está também na declaração dele" -- the whole line's output, of which a sibling's
#    slice is that sibling's demand in its own filing. A rule reading "a supply cannot serve
#    more than was asked" would fire on a correct document. The bound that holds is the
#    supply's own, and it is in checks/draw_exceeds_the_supply.sqlc.
#
# ⛔ A DRAW AGAINST NO RATING IS NO ROW. `refutation/object-storage` draws 47 with its amount
#   filed `notApplicable`; utilisation of a rating nobody stated is unanswerable, not zero.
#   layers/absorber.sqlc states the principle.
#
# ⚠️ `capacity_slack` IS LEFT NULL WHERE IT IS UNMEASURED rather than coalesced to zero. Six of
#   these layers do not know how far they can stretch, and a nameplate is not a ceiling until
#   somebody says the buffer is empty.
-- pm:Supply/pm:Jagged/pm:draw against pm:Nameplate/pm:amount and pm:Nameplate/pm:capacitySlack.
SELECT n.filing, n.layer,
       n.draw_low, n.draw_mode, n.draw_high, n.draw_unit,
       n.amount_low  AS n_low,
       n.amount_mode AS n_mode,
       n.amount_high AS n_high,
       n.amount_unit AS n_unit,
       s.mode   AS capacity_slack,
       s.absent AS capacity_absent
FROM pm.nameplate n
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(entries/slacks.sqlc)
) s ON s.filing = n.filing AND s.layer = n.layer AND s.buffer = 'capacity'
WHERE n.draw_mode   IS NOT NULL
  AND n.amount_mode IS NOT NULL
